
# ==============================================================================
# [NOTE] Mosquitto Password File Template (passwd.example)
#
# Role: Provides an example format of the credential file required by Mosquitto.
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Do NOT put real passwords in this file! This file IS tracked by Git.
# - The real file MUST be named `passwd` in this directory (which is git-ignored).
#
# How credentials are generated:
# Mosquitto requires passwords to be hashed (SHA512-PBKDF2).
#
# Method 1 (Recommended): Use the provided Dockerized helper script:
#   ./scripts/setup-mosquitto-auth.sh <username> <password>
#
# Method 2: Use Docker one-off command:
#   docker run --rm -v $(pwd)/mosquitto/config:/config eclipse-mosquitto \
#     mosquitto_passwd -c -b /config/passwd <username> <password>
#
# Method 3: If `mosquitto_passwd` is installed locally:
#   mosquitto_passwd -c passwd <username>
# ==============================================================================

# Example placeholder entry (do not use for production):
# Format: username:password_hash
legacy_admin:$7$101$placeholder_hash_only_do_not_use$randomstring==
